And Moses
returned unto the Lord, and said, Oh, this people have sinned a great sin,
and have made them gods of gold. Yet now, if thou wilt forgive their sins—;
and if not, blot me, I pray thee, out of thy book which thou hast written. And the Lord said unto Moses, Whosoever hath sinned against me, him will
I blot out of my book." (Ex. 32:15-35; 33:13; 34:9; Deut. 5:5; 9:24-29;
10:10; Ps. 106:23.)
